---
import EnterpriseDetail from '../../components/enterprise/EnterpriseDetail.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/ComparisonTable.astro';
---

<EnterpriseDetail
  slug="compliance"
  seoTitle="Data and Credentials | SAM Enterprise"
  seoDescription="Where a self-hosted SAM installation stores data, how it encrypts credentials, and which cloud account runs your agents."
  title="Where your data lives"
  subtitle="A SAM installation runs in your own Cloudflare account, and agents run on cloud machines you connect. There is no hosted SAM service holding your data."
>
  <h2>What is stored where</h2>
  <ComparisonTable
    caption="Storage in a self-hosted installation. Everything in the first five rows is in the Cloudflare account you deploy to."
    rowHeader="Data"
    columns={['Stored in', 'Notes']}
    rows={[
      { label: 'Users, projects, tasks, settings', cells: ['Cloudflare D1', 'Point-in-time restore for 30 days through the D1 restore workflow.'] },
      { label: 'Chat messages, tool calls, activity', cells: ['Durable Objects (SQLite), one per project', 'Large tool output is archived to R2.'] },
      { label: 'Credentials', cells: ['Cloudflare D1', 'Encrypted with AES-256-GCM, unique IV per credential.'] },
      { label: 'Workspace snapshots', cells: ['Cloudflare R2', 'Home directory and uncommitted work, so a session can sleep and wake.'] },
      { label: 'Files, logs, diagnostics', cells: ['Cloudflare R2', 'Project library files, node logs and debug packages.'] },
      { label: 'Source code being worked on', cells: ['The workspace machine', 'Pushed to GitHub or GitLab when the agent pushes.'] },
      { label: 'Prompts and code context', cells: ['Your model provider', 'Sent directly by the agent, or through the installation AI proxy if you opt in.'] },
    ]}
  />
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Cloudflare is part of your trust boundary.</strong> The control plane, chat history and snapshots
      live in Cloudflare, a US company with a global network. SAM cannot yet store chat history in a database
      outside Cloudflare.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Which cloud account runs agents</h2>
  <p>
    For each machine, SAM uses the project's cloud credential if it has one, then the user's own, then a
    credential the installation administrator connected for everyone. An administrator who connects no
    installation credential makes every user or project bring their own.
  </p>
  <p>
    With no cloud credential at all, a profile can still run Instant sessions on Cloudflare Containers in your
    Cloudflare account. Those do not use your devcontainer or run Docker.
  </p>

  <h2>How credentials are protected</h2>
  <p>
    Cloud tokens, agent API keys and subscription tokens are each encrypted with AES-256-GCM and their own random
    IV, under an installation encryption key held as a Cloudflare Worker secret. They are never stored as
    environment variables.
  </p>
  <p>
    Agent credentials can be personal or pinned to a project or profile. SAM looks for a project credential
    first, then the user's. An inactive project credential blocks the lookup instead of silently falling back to
    a broader one.
  </p>
  <ComparisonTable
    caption="Credential scopes."
    rowHeader="Credential"
    columns={['Scope', 'Reaches machines?']}
    rows={[
      { label: 'Cloud provider tokens', cells: ['Per user, per project, or installation-wide', 'No. The control plane calls the provider API.'] },
      { label: 'Agent API keys', cells: ['Per user, pinned to projects or profiles', 'Yes, injected into the workspace when the agent starts.'] },
      { label: 'Subscription tokens', cells: ['Per user, pinned to projects or profiles', 'Yes, injected into the workspace when the agent starts.'] },
    ]}
  />

  <h2>Deploying it yourself</h2>
  <p>
    Follow the <a href="/docs/guides/self-hosting/">self-hosting guide</a>, where GitHub Actions and Pulumi deploy
    SAM to your Cloudflare account, or use the <a href="/docs/guides/installer/">browser installer</a>, which is
    newer and still labelled experimental and takes about half an hour. An update workflow brings later
    releases in.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once installed, SAM runs only in your Cloudflare account and the cloud accounts you connect. The hosted
    installer holds a short-lived Cloudflare token while it works; you can host the installer yourself instead.
  </p>
</EnterpriseDetail>
